  "caption": "Quinn's feet felt like walking on sand, toes burned at night, and turning off the lights meant an instant wobble.\n\nThe long nerves to the feet can become less sensitive, so the brain gets less information about where your feet are. That makes balance harder, especially in the dark when your eyes can't help.\n\nWhat often helps: challenging balance practice with support nearby, checking your feet every day, wearing shoes rather than socks or bare feet, and lighting up the night path at home. Your GP can check for causes that may be treatable.\n\nNumbness that spreads over days or weeks, one side clearly worse, foot drop, or a new foot wound should be checked promptly.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
